  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-usage-plus",
      "text": "[中文](README.zh.md) | English\n\nIndependent DSH usage and official Plan-quota plugin (Host + Web UI). It does not pin a DSH version: optional UI surfaces activate only when the running DSH exposes the required capabilities."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-usage-plus",
      "text": "- Reuses credentials already configured for DSH model providers.\n- Shows real 5-hour, weekly, and monthly windows on `conversation.composer.dock` (alongside StatsPills / ContextMeter).\n- Labels every Plugins-page number with its scope (`全设备` / `账号级` / `本会话`) so device-wide totals never read as session totals.\n- Renders nothing when a provider exposes no official quota window.\n- Keeps CPAMC and Volcano Ark as separate sources (Plugins page → Settings).\n- Overview includes a full 26-week Mon–Sun activity heatmap (ledger default 182 days).\n- Keeps all secrets in the host process / credential vault."
    },
    {
      "section": "Composer plan strip (current model)",
      "text": "When the active model matches an official plan source, the composer dock shows real 5-hour / weekly / monthly windows. Hover for reset times and the source chip (for example Volcano). Nothing is rendered when the remote API exposes no official window."
    },
    {
      "section": "Plugins → Usage · Overview",
      "text": "The overview summarizes today and the last 30 days, cache hit rate, token buckets, and per-provider totals. The balance card only lists real balances. Plan quotas and external sources live on the other tabs of the same Plugins page."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Install into a DSH profile with the official plugin command (adds the dependency and appends the package to `dsh.profile.bundles` so `cordis.patch.yml` is applied):\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add ./"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-usage-plus",
      "text": "```\n\nThe package ships its own bundle patch (`id: usage-plus`, `name: dsh-usage-plus`).\nIf the older `@linxin666/dsh-usage` / `web-ui-usage` row is also present, disable it\nin the profile patch to avoid duplicate UI.\n\nOptional credential names are `CPAMC_MANAGEMENT_KEY`, `VOLC_ACCESSKEY`, and `VOLC_SECRETKEY`. Enable the matching source under **Plugins → Usage Statistics → Settings**, then **Save**. Leaving the page discards an unsaved draft (official `plugins.item` contract)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Model Experience",
      "text": "- Quota strip follows the **session** `modelSelection` projection (composer picker / `/model`). It does not fall through to another session’s or the global plan while this session already has a route.\n- Windows are only shown when the remote Plan API returns real percentages; there is no local token estimate disguised as quota.\n- Token ledger and balance cards stay on the Plugins page; they do not inject into the conversation transcript."
    },
    {
      "section": "Known Limitations",
      "text": "- DSH versions are not pinned. Missing optional surfaces (`configForms`, `plugins.item`, `conversation.composer.dock`) are treated as unavailable capabilities instead of a startup failure.\n- Providers without an official Plan API show no strip and no fabricated windows.\n- CPAMC accepts loopback origins (or hosts listed in `cpamcAllowedHosts`) only; management routes are read-only and reject redirects.\n- Volcano Ark needs vaulted AK/SK (or `VOLC_ACCESSKEY` / `VOLC_SECRETKEY`); signing runs only in the Host process.\n- Floating pet bubble announcements need a separate pet service in the profile; `bubbleMode: off` disables them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Accuracy",
      "text": "Plan UI and the composer strip only display windows returned by official remote APIs. Missing Plan API, missing percentages, or probe failures are never replaced with local estimates."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Based on `@linxin666/dsh-usage` (Apache-2.0). CPAMC security constraints and Volcano signing behavior reference `dsh-cost-meter` (MIT). See [LICENSE](LICENSE)."
    }
  ],
